{"assets":["/statement-assets/0e958f3b8b34be6d28ab89ce104411c770e9760f8a37de62956a6ec8425ce3a2.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1286","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Harry The Potter"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"9 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To defeat Lord Voldemort, Harry needs to destroy all horcruxes first. The last horcrux is an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers, which also needs to be destroyed. The array is considered destroyed if all its elements are zeroes. To destroy the array, Harry can perform two types of operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose an index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$), an integer $$$x$$$, and subtract $$$x$$$ from $$$a_i$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose two indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ ($$$1 \\le i, j \\le n; i \\ne j$$$), an integer $$$x$$$, and subtract $$$x$$$ from $$$a_i$$$ and $$$x + 1$$$ from $$$a_j$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that $$$x$$$ does not have to be positive."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0e958f3b8b34be6d28ab89ce104411c770e9760f8a37de62956a6ec8425ce3a2.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Harry is in a hurry, please help him to find the minimum number of operations required to destroy the array and exterminate Lord Voldemort."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ — the size of the array $$$a$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 20$$$). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ — array elements ($$$-10^{15} \\le a_i \\le 10^{15}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the minimum number of operations required to destroy the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 10 100\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n5 3 -2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example one can just apply the operation of the first kind three times."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, one can apply the operation of the second kind two times: first, choose $$$i = 2, j = 1, x = 4$$$, it transforms the array into $$$(0, -1, -2)$$$, and then choose $$$i = 3, j = 2, x = -2$$$ to destroy the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, there is nothing to be done, since the array is already destroyed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1286F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1286/problem/F"}